      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T07:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A comment explaining this would be helpful.\n\nInstead of inserting at hard-coded string index \"4\", can we search for \"-\" in the `l_mapKey` string and then insert the `l_nodeId` after that?\nThis way, if in future \"Ufcs\" string length changes, we wouldn\u0027t need to refactor this code.",
      "revId": "832f1ae88f52a8d1d814096cdb59294fbca5613b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d23a061_dcff6967",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/src/config_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T08:06:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The LOC will be more if I follow this approach , As stated incase in future if Ufcs string length changes that can be updated in constants file and we need to just use the same expression here in place of `\"constants::VALUE_4\"` .\nAlso one thing If I go via this approach, I have to also explicitly handle the Loc. code where there is no dash character \"-\" such as `\"Ufcs\"`",
      "parentUuid": "ab2b14d6_82beeed3",
      "revId": "832f1ae88f52a8d1d814096cdb59294fbca5613b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c60afe0_df79d3ee",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/src/config_manager.cpp",
