    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "927804b2_e2b5c608",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/src/config_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T07:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With this change, `m_unexpandedLocCodeToInvPathsMap` will have entries where each node qualified unexpanded location code maps to a unique inventory path.\n\nCurrently, `m_unexpandedLocCodeToInvPathsMap` is of type `    std::unordered_map\u003cstd::string, types::ListOfPaths\u003e`, where each map unexpanded location code maps to a list of paths. Do we still need to maintain this data structure format where the map values are a list of paths?",
      "revId": "832f1ae88f52a8d1d814096cdb59294fbca5613b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d57dfb83_07c8e676",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/src/config_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T08:06:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This map is used by the api `getFrusByUnexpandedLocationCode` and it returns types::ListOfPaths as its D-Bus contract. Changing the map value type means we still have to reconstruct a single-element list at the return boundary — so the gain is minimal and adds a conversion. The current ListOfPaths type keeps the getter trivial (return l_it-\u003esecond with no wrapping),",
      "parentUuid": "927804b2_e2b5c608",
      "revId": "832f1ae88f52a8d1d814096cdb59294fbca5613b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f70c52e7_ea9442c9",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/src/config_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T08:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree about the API \u0027s \"D-Bus contract\". But with this change, we are unnecessarily maintaining a list of paths, which unnecessarily consumes more memory at runtime. \n\nAlso, if any entry already exists in the map with key \u003d\u003d `l_mapKey`, we are overriding it instead of appending to the existing list.",
      "parentUuid": "d57dfb83_07c8e676",
      "revId": "832f1ae88f52a8d1d814096cdb59294fbca5613b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
